{"id": "de667add-23da-496b-9118-479b50d4a9c6", "slug": "vortex-system", "title": "Vortex System", "description": "Vortex System Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"Vortex System\"\ndescription: \"Vortex System Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#D4FF00\"\n  secondary: \"#000000\"\n  accent: \"#D4FF00\"\n  background: \"#000000\"\n  surface: \"#18181B\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"2px\"\n  control: \"2px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Vortex System\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 182; favorites: 10; remixes: 1.\nTags: background, animated, dither, effect, webgl.\n## Overview\nVortex System Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\n\nAbsolute Synchronization Distributing compute and state across decentralized node clusters shouldn't require latency trade-offs or trust delegates. [ VORTEX // CORE ] CLUSTER Engineered for scale. Controlled by none. Co…\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Absolute Synchronization; Engineered for scale. Controlled by none.; As computational power decentralizes, the need for a unified consensus layer is absolute; Zero latency. Zero friction..\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #D4FF00, secondary #000000, accent #D4FF00, background #000000, surface #18181B, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and JetBrains Mono for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Vortex System</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <!-- GSAP for animations -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n    \n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <style>\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;\n            background-color: #111111;\n            color: #000000;\n            -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n            -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n        }\n        .font-mono {\n            font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;\n        }\n        /* Custom noise overlay to match reference texture */\n        .noise-overlay {\n            position: fixed;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: 100vw;\n            height: 100vh;\n            pointer-events: none;\n            z-index: 50;\n            opacity: 0.04;\n            background-image: url(\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 200 200' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noiseFilter'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.85' numOctaves='3' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noiseFilter)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\");\n        }\n        .brand-acid {\n            background-color: #D4FF00;\n        }\n        /* Fix for masked reveal clipping descenders slightly */\n        .reveal-mask {\n            display: inline-block;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            vertical-align: bottom;\n            padding-bottom: 0.1em; \n            margin-bottom: -0.1em;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body class=\"min-h-screen p-2 md:p-4 lg:p-6 relative\">\n    <div class=\"noise-overlay\"></div>\n\n    <main class=\"max-w-[2000px] mx-auto w-full h-full grid grid-cols-1 xl:grid-cols-2 gap-2 md:gap-4 lg:gap-6 relative z-10\">\n        \n        <!-- Quadrant 1 -->\n        <article class=\"brand-acid rounded-[2px] p-6 md:p-8 lg:p-10 flex flex-col relative overflow-hidden min-h-[450px] lg:min-h-[500px]\">\n            <div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-start z-10 gap-6\">\n                <h1 class=\"reveal-target text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight uppercase max-w-xl leading-[0.95]\">Absolute Synchronization</h1>\n                <p class=\"text-xs md:text-sm max-w-[280px] md:text-right leading-relaxed font-medium\">Distributing compute and state across decentralized node clusters shouldn't require latency trade-offs or trust delegates.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 top-[140px] pointer-events-none\">\n                <canvas id=\"canvas-1\" class=\"w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n            </div>\n        </article>\n\n        <!-- Quadrant 2 -->\n        <article class=\"brand-acid rounded-[2px] p-6 md:p-8 lg:p-10 flex flex-col relative overflow-hidden min-h-[450px] lg:min-h-[500px]\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between font-mono text-[10px] md:text-xs uppercase tracking-widest z-10 mb-10 md:mb-16\">\n                <span>[ VORTEX // CORE ]</span>\n                <span class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-black block\"></span> CLUSTER</span>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"flex flex-col lg:flex-row z-10 relative h-full gap-8\">\n                <div class=\"w-full lg:w-5/12 flex flex-col\">\n                    <h2 class=\"reveal-target text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight uppercase mb-8 leading-[0.95]\">Engineered for scale.<br>Controlled by none.</h2>\n                    <div class=\"space-y-6 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium\">\n                        <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Compute is fragmented across isolated server farms, forcing inefficient processing and localized bottlenecks globally.</p>\n                        <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Legacy architectures introduce latency, single points of failure, and rigid scaling limitations.</p>\n                        <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Modern systems require fluid resource distribution, not disjointed processing units.</p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"w-full lg:w-7/12 absolute lg:relative inset-0 lg:inset-auto opacity-20 lg:opacity-100 pointer-events-none flex items-center justify-end\">\n                    <canvas id=\"canvas-2\" class=\"w-full h-full absolute right-0 scale-150 lg:scale-100 origin-right\"></canvas>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"absolute bottom-6 md:bottom-10 left-6 md:left-10 z-10\">\n                <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:hamburger-menu-linear\" class=\"text-3xl\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></iconify-icon>\n            </div>\n        </article>\n\n        <!-- Quadrant 3 -->\n        <article class=\"brand-acid rounded-[2px] p-6 md:p-8 lg:p-10 flex flex-col relative overflow-hidden min-h-[450px] lg:min-h-[500px]\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between font-mono text-[10px] md:text-xs uppercase tracking-widest z-10 mb-8\">\n                <span>[ VORTEX.SYS ]</span>\n                <span class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-black block\"></span> CONSENSUS</span>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"flex flex-col lg:flex-row justify-between items-start z-10 mb-12 gap-8\">\n                <h2 class=\"reveal-target text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] font-semibold tracking-tight uppercase max-w-2xl leading-[0.95]\">As computational power decentralizes, the need for a unified consensus layer is absolute</h2>\n                <p class=\"text-xs md:text-sm max-w-[300px] lg:text-right leading-relaxed font-medium shrink-0 pt-2\">As networks expand, datasets, users, and nodes are distributed globally. The next phase isn't multi-cloud — it's ubiquitous compute.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"relative flex-grow min-h-[200px] mt-auto\">\n                <canvas id=\"canvas-3\" class=\"absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-full w-full pointer-events-none\"></canvas>\n            </div>\n        </article>\n\n        <!-- Quadrant 4 -->\n        <article class=\"brand-acid rounded-[2px] p-6 md:p-8 lg:p-10 flex flex-col relative overflow-hidden min-h-[450px] lg:min-h-[500px]\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between font-mono text-[10px] md:text-xs uppercase tracking-widest z-10 mb-8\">\n                <span>[ VORTEX // INFRA ]</span>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"flex flex-col xl:flex-row items-start z-10 mb-10 gap-8 xl:gap-16\">\n                <h2 class=\"reveal-target text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight uppercase leading-[0.95] whitespace-nowrap\">Zero latency.<br>Zero friction.</h2>\n                <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium w-full xl:pt-2\">\n                    <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Data is isolated across databases, forcing slow queries and state fragmentation.</p>\n                    <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Standard methods introduce overhead, downtime risks, and broken data pipelines.</p>\n                    <p class=\"leading-relaxed\">Platforms need synchronous replication, not disjointed storage layers.</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"relative flex-grow min-h-[220px]\">\n                <canvas id=\"canvas-4\" class=\"absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-full w-full pointer-events-none\"></canvas>\n            </div>\n        </article>\n\n    </main>\n\n    <script>\n        // Utility for managing canvas animations and scaling\n        class CanvasSystem {\n            constructor(id, drawFn) {\n                this.canvas = document.getElementById(id);\n                if (!this.canvas) return;\n                this.ctx = this.canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: false });\n                this.drawFn = drawFn;\n                this.time = Math.random() * 100;\n                \n                this.resize();\n                window.addEventListener('resize', () => this.resize());\n                this.animate();\n            }\n\n            resize() {\n                const rect = this.canvas.parentElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n                const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n                this.canvas.width = rect.width * dpr;\n                this.canvas.height = rect.height * dpr;\n                this.ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\n                this.width = rect.width;\n                this.height = rect.height;\n            }\n\n            animate() {\n                this.time += 0.015;\n                // Use brand acid background to prevent artifacting with alpha: false\n                this.ctx.fillStyle = '#D4FF00';\n                this.ctx.fillRect(0, 0, this.width, this.height);\n                this.drawFn(this.ctx, this.width, this.height, this.time);\n                requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Canvas 1: Speed Lines (Diagonal moving dashes)\n        new CanvasSystem('canvas-1', (ctx, w, h, t) => {\n            ctx.strokeStyle = '#000000';\n            const rowHeight = 14;\n            const bandSpacing = 160;\n            const dashLength = 30;\n            const speed = 120;\n\n            for (let y = 0; y < h; y += rowHeight) {\n                // Base thin lines\n                ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.moveTo(0, y);\n                ctx.lineTo(w, y);\n                ctx.stroke();\n\n                // Thick moving diagonal segments\n                ctx.lineWidth = rowHeight - 4;\n                ctx.lineCap = 'butt';\n                for (let x = -w; x < w * 2; x += dashLength) {\n                    // Create diagonal bands\n                    const offset = (x + y * 2.5 - t * speed);\n                    const mod = ((offset % bandSpacing) + bandSpacing) % bandSpacing;\n                    \n                    if (mod < 60) {\n                        ctx.beginPath();\n                        ctx.moveTo(x, y);\n                        ctx.lineTo(x + dashLength - 4, y);\n                        ctx.stroke();\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Canvas 2: Globe/Circle Visualization\n        new CanvasSystem('canvas-2', (ctx, w, h, t) => {\n            ctx.fillStyle = '#000000';\n            const cx = w * 0.6; // Offset slightly to right as per ref\n            const cy = h / 2;\n            const radius = Math.min(w, h) * 0.45;\n            const lineSpacing = 16;\n            const speed = 2;\n\n            for (let x = 0; x < w; x += lineSpacing) {\n                const distFromCenter = Math.abs(x - cx);\n                if (distFromCenter < radius) {\n                    // Calculate height of line within circle\n                    const yExtents = Math.sqrt(radius * radius - distFromCenter * distFromCenter);\n                    \n                    // Base thin line\n                    ctx.fillRect(x, cy - yExtents, 2, yExtents * 2);\n\n                    // Animated thick segments pulsing through\n                    const phase = x * 0.05 + t * speed;\n                    const thickVal = (Math.sin(phase) + Math.sin(phase * 1.5)) / 2;\n                    \n                    if (thickVal > 0.3) {\n                        const thickHeight = yExtents * thickVal;\n                        const blockYOffset = Math.sin(t * 0.5 + x * 0.1) * (yExtents * 0.3); // Shift block up/down\n                        \n                        let startY = cy - thickHeight / 2 + blockYOffset;\n                        let endY = cy + thickHeight / 2 + blockYOffset;\n                        \n                        // Clamp to circle bounds\n                        startY = Math.max(startY, cy - yExtents);\n                        endY = Math.min(endY, cy + yExtents);\n\n                        ctx.fillRect(x - 2, startY, 6, endY - startY);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Canvas 3: Barcode / Execution Spectrum\n        new CanvasSystem('canvas-3', (ctx, w, h, t) => {\n            ctx.fillStyle = '#000000';\n            const lineSpacing = 12;\n            const blockWidth = w * 0.7;\n            const startX = (w - blockWidth) / 2;\n            const endX = startX + blockWidth;\n            \n            for (let x = 0; x < w; x += lineSpacing) {\n                // Background tall thin lines\n                const baseHeight = h * 0.8;\n                ctx.fillRect(x, (h - baseHeight) / 2, 1.5, baseHeight);\n\n                // Central heavy block with slight equalizer animation\n                if (x > startX && x < endX) {\n                    // Create varying block heights\n                    const noise = Math.sin(x * 0.02) * Math.cos(x * 0.05 + t);\n                    const blockHeight = h * 0.5 + (noise * h * 0.1);\n                    \n                    // Thicken the line\n                    ctx.fillRect(x - 3, (h - blockHeight) / 2, 7.5, blockHeight);\n                }\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Canvas 4: Data Fragment Grid\n        new CanvasSystem('canvas-4', (ctx, w, h, t) => {\n            ctx.fillStyle = '#000000';\n            const cols = Math.floor(w / 14);\n            const rows = Math.floor(h / 18);\n            const spacingX = w / cols;\n            const spacingY = h / rows;\n\n            for (let i = 0; i < cols; i++) {\n                for (let j = 0; j < rows; j++) {\n                    const x = i * spacingX;\n                    const y = j * spacingY;\n                    \n                    // Base small dash\n                    ctx.fillRect(x, y + 4, 1.5, 6);\n\n                    // Determine if this cell should have a heavier/longer mark based on a slow moving wave\n                    const wave1 = Math.sin(i * 0.2 + t * 0.8);\n                    const wave2 = Math.cos(j * 0.3 - t * 1.2);\n                    const threshold = (wave1 + wave2) / 2;\n\n                    // Clusters of thick lines on the left side, thinning out\n                    const falloff = 1 - (i / cols); \n\n                    if (threshold > 0.2 || (Math.random() > 0.98 && falloff > 0.5)) {\n                         // Only draw thick blocks primarily on the upper/left diagonal pattern as seen in ref\n                         if((i + j * 0.5) < (cols * 0.8)) {\n                             ctx.fillRect(x - 1, y, 3.5, 14);\n                         }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        });\n\n        // GSAP Masked Stagger Reveal Logic\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n            gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n            // Function to split text into word chunks safely preserving HTML like <br>\n            function wrapWords(el) {\n                const temp = document.createElement('div');\n                el.childNodes.forEach(node => {\n                    if (node.nodeType === 3) { // Text node\n                        const words = node.nodeValue.split(/(\\s+)/);\n                        words.forEach(word => {\n                            if (word.trim() === '') {\n                                temp.appendChild(document.createTextNode(word));\n                            } else {\n                                const outer = document.createElement('span');\n                                outer.className = 'reveal-mask';\n                                \n                                const inner = document.createElement('span');\n                                inner.style.display = 'inline-block';\n                                inner.style.transform = 'translateY(110%)';\n                                inner.className = 'reveal-word';\n                                inner.innerText = word;\n                                \n                                outer.appendChild(inner);\n                                temp.appendChild(outer);\n                            }\n                        });\n                    } else if (node.nodeType === 1) { // Element node (e.g. <br>)\n                        temp.appendChild(node.cloneNode(true));\n                    }\n                });\n                el.innerHTML = temp.innerHTML;\n            }\n\n            document.querySelectorAll('.reveal-target').forEach(heading => {\n                wrapWords(heading);\n                \n                gsap.to(heading.querySelectorAll('.reveal-word'), {\n                    y: \"0%\",\n                    duration: 0.8,\n                    stagger: 0.04,\n                    ease: \"power3.out\",\n                    scrollTrigger: {\n                        trigger: heading,\n                        start: \"top 90%\",\n                        toggleActions: \"play none none reverse\"\n                    }\n                });\n            });\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "vortex-system.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/vortex-system.jpg", "source_name": "vortex-system-DESIGN.md", "views": 216, "forks": 2, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-06-12T07:38:10.793894+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T23:42:18.058324+00:00"}